  "generated_text": "First, we need to factor the quadratic expression \\(12y^2 - 65y + 42\\).\n\nWe start by factoring out the greatest common factor (GCF) from the expression:\n\\[\n12y^2 - 65y + 42 = 12(y^2 - 5y + 3)\n\\]\n\nNext, we factor the quadratic expression \\(y^2 - 5y + 3\\):\n\\[\ny^2 - 5y + 3 = (y - 1)(y - 3)\n\\]\n\nSo, the factored form of the original expression is:\n\\[\n12(y - 1)(y - 3)\n\\]\n\nWe can write this as \\((Ay - 14)(By - 3)\\), where \\(A = 12\\) and \\(B = 1\\).\n\nNow, we calculate \\(AB + A\\):\n\\[\nAB + A = 12 \\cdot 1 + 12 = 12 + 12 = 24\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{24}\\).",
